div.p:
(1) first use of herbicides in war except use, under regulations applicable to
                    their domestic use, for control of vegetation within U.S. bases and
                    installations or around their immediate defensive perimeters;

(b) Use of riot control agents in situations where civilian casualties can be
                    reduced or avoided. This use would be restricted to situations in which
                    civilians are used to mask or screen attacks;

(c) Use of riot control agents in rescue missions. The use of riot control agents
                    would be permissible in the recovery of remotely isolated personnel such as
                    downed aircrews—and passengers;
